Instructions for Authors of Accepted Papers:
Authors must carefully follow the instructions below while preparing and submitting the final (camera-ready) paper.


An individual may not be listed as an author or co-author on more than TWO registered papers. Authors must confirm that all author names, affiliations, and email addresses are correct. The authors are solely responsible for any incorrect or mismatched information.

Author details must be uniformly formatted and should include only: Name, Department, Organization, City, Country, and Email Address (Do not include salutations, titles, or designations.)
Ensure that all references cited in the manuscript appear in the reference list, and that all references strictly follow the IEEE referencing format.
All figures, tables, and equations must be original. If any content is reused or adapted, proper citation is mandatory.
Authors are responsible for maintaining the technical quality, clarity, and professionalism of the paper. All reviewer comments must be fully addressed in the camera-ready version.
Papers must strictly follow the IEEE conference format. Authors must use the official IEEE templates available at:https://www.ieee.org/conferences/publishing/templates.html
The maximum page limit is 6 pages. Over-length papers of up to 8 pages are permitted with additional charges.
The abstract should concisely summarize the motivation, methodology, and key results.
The introduction must clearly define the problem statement and research objectives.
Authors must explicitly highlight the novelty and main contributions of their work.

Important Notes
No changes to authorship or paper content are allowed after final submission. The maximum number of authors allowed in the camera-ready paper is six. Any mistake in the camera-ready submission may lead to rejection of the paper.
Similarity checks Requirements:
Overall similarity must be less than 10% (excluding references) and less than 15% (including references).
Similarity from any single source must not exceed 2%.
AI-generated content is strictly prohibited (must be 0% not *%).
Any violation of IEEE plagiarism policies, detected at any stage of the publication process, shall lead to immediate rejection of the paper without refund and without any prior intimation to the authors.